<sect1 id="whpg-live-query-plan">
 <title>Live Query Plan Viewer</title>

 <indexterm zone="whpg-live-query-plan">
  <primary>whpg_live_query_plan</primary>
 </indexterm>

 <para>
  WarehousePG provides a set of functions for inspecting the current
  execution plan and runtime metrics of a query running on the coordinator
  backend.  This is useful for diagnosing long-running queries without
  interrupting them.
 </para>

 <sect2 id="whpg-live-query-plan-overview">
  <title>Overview</title>

  <para>
   The live query plan feature consists of two SQL functions and a
   persistent history table:
  </para>

  <itemizedlist>
   <listitem>
    <para>
     <function>pg_catalog.whpg_live_query_plan(pid int4)</function>
     returns the current execution plan with per-node, per-segment
     runtime counters for the query running on backend <parameter>pid</parameter>.
    </para>
   </listitem>
   <listitem>
    <para>
     <function>pg_catalog.whpg_collect_segment_metrics(ssid int4, ccnt int4)</function>
     is an internal function dispatched to each segment to collect
     per-node <structname>InstrumentationSlot</structname> data.
     It is not intended for direct use.
    </para>
   </listitem>
   <listitem>
    <para>
     <structname>pg_catalog.whpg_query_history</structname> stores
     end-of-query per-node execution metrics written asynchronously by
     the <literal>whpg history writer</literal> background worker.
    </para>
   </listitem>
  </itemizedlist>

  <para>
   The live view is pull-only and read-only.  It does not interrupt the
   running query.  Counter values are approximate: a node that is
   currently executing shows its last completed-cycle value.
  </para>
 </sect2>

 <sect2 id="whpg-live-query-plan-prerequisites">
  <title>Prerequisites</title>

  <para>
   The GUC <varname>gp_enable_query_metrics</varname> must be
   <literal>on</literal> (the default since this feature was introduced).
   With it off the plan registry is not populated and both functions
   return empty result sets.
  </para>
 </sect2>

 <sect2 id="whpg-live-query-plan-functions">
  <title>Functions</title>

  <refentry id="whpg-live-query-plan-func">
   <refmeta>
    <refentrytitle>whpg_live_query_plan</refentrytitle>
   </refmeta>

   <refnamediv>
    <refname>whpg_live_query_plan</refname>
    <refpurpose>return the live execution plan with per-segment metrics
    for a running query</refpurpose>
   </refnamediv>

   <refsynopsisdiv>
    <synopsis>
pg_catalog.whpg_live_query_plan(pid int4)
RETURNS TABLE (
    slice_id        int4,
    plan_node_id    int4,
    parent_node_id  int4,
    node_type       text,
    segindex        int4,
    plan_rows       float8,
    running         boolean,
    tuples          int8,
    ntuples_total   int8,
    actual_ms       float8,
    execmem_bytes   int8,
    workmem_bytes   int8,
    spill_bytes     int8,
    bufusage_blocks int8
)
    </synopsis>
   </refsynopsisdiv>

   <refsect1>
    <title>Description</title>

    <para>
     <function>whpg_live_query_plan</function> returns one row per
     <literal>(plan node, segment)</literal> pair for the query currently
     executing on the coordinator backend identified by
     <parameter>pid</parameter>.  If no query is running for that backend,
     the function returns an empty set.
    </para>

    <para>
     The function first reads the compact plan tree from the shared-memory
     plan registry, then fans out
     <function>whpg_collect_segment_metrics</function> to every segment
     on a fresh gang so the running query is not interrupted.
     Coordinator-local metrics use <literal>segindex = -1</literal>.
    </para>
   </refsect1>

   <refsect1>
    <title>Arguments</title>
    <variablelist>
     <varlistentry>
      <term><parameter>pid</parameter></term>
      <listitem>
       <para>
        The OS process ID of the coordinator backend running the target
        query.  Use <literal>pg_stat_activity.pid</literal> to find it.
       </para>
      </listitem>
     </varlistentry>
    </variablelist>
   </refsect1>

   <refsect1>
    <title>Return Columns</title>
    <informaltable>
     <tgroup cols="3">
      <thead>
       <row>
        <entry>Column</entry>
        <entry>Type</entry>
        <entry>Description</entry>
       </row>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
       <row><entry>slice_id</entry><entry>int4</entry>
        <entry>Execution slice the node belongs to.</entry></row>
       <row><entry>plan_node_id</entry><entry>int4</entry>
        <entry>Unique node identifier within this query.</entry></row>
       <row><entry>parent_node_id</entry><entry>int4</entry>
        <entry>Node ID of the parent; <literal>-1</literal> for the root.</entry></row>
       <row><entry>node_type</entry><entry>text</entry>
        <entry>Human-readable plan node name (e.g., <literal>Seq Scan</literal>).</entry></row>
       <row><entry>segindex</entry><entry>int4</entry>
        <entry>Segment that produced this row; <literal>-1</literal> for the coordinator.</entry></row>
       <row><entry>plan_rows</entry><entry>float8</entry>
        <entry>Optimizer row-count estimate.</entry></row>
       <row><entry>running</entry><entry>boolean</entry>
        <entry>True if the node is currently executing.</entry></row>
       <row><entry>tuples</entry><entry>int8</entry>
        <entry>Tuples emitted so far on this segment.</entry></row>
       <row><entry>ntuples_total</entry><entry>int8</entry>
        <entry>Tuples summed across all segments for this node.</entry></row>
       <row><entry>actual_ms</entry><entry>float8</entry>
        <entry>Elapsed execution time in milliseconds.</entry></row>
       <row><entry>execmem_bytes</entry><entry>int8</entry>
        <entry>Executor memory used (bytes).</entry></row>
       <row><entry>workmem_bytes</entry><entry>int8</entry>
        <entry>Work memory used (bytes).</entry></row>
       <row><entry>spill_bytes</entry><entry>int8</entry>
        <entry>Bytes written to workfiles (spill to disk).</entry></row>
       <row><entry>bufusage_blocks</entry><entry>int8</entry>
        <entry>Shared buffer blocks hit and read.</entry></row>
      </tbody>
     </tgroup>
    </informaltable>
   </refsect1>

   <refsect1>
    <title>Permissions</title>
    <para>
     Superusers may inspect any backend.  Non-superusers may only inspect
     backends that they own (same role as the target backend's
     <literal>usesysid</literal>).  Attempting to inspect another user's
     backend raises <errorcode>ERRCODE_INSUFFICIENT_PRIVILEGE</errorcode>.
    </para>
   </refsect1>

   <refsect1>
    <title>Example</title>
    <programlisting>
-- Find the PID of a long-running query
SELECT pid, query
FROM pg_stat_activity
WHERE state = 'active' AND pid &lt;&gt; pg_backend_pid();

-- Inspect its live plan
SELECT slice_id, plan_node_id, node_type, segindex,
       tuples, actual_ms, spill_bytes
FROM pg_catalog.whpg_live_query_plan(12345)
ORDER BY slice_id, plan_node_id, segindex;
    </programlisting>
   </refsect1>
  </refentry>
 </sect2>

 <sect2 id="whpg-query-history">
  <title>Query History Table</title>

  <para>
   At the end of every query (subject to GUC settings),
   <productname>WarehousePG</productname> enqueues one row per plan node
   into a shared-memory ring buffer.  The
   <literal>whpg history writer</literal> background worker drains this
   buffer and inserts rows into
   <structname>pg_catalog.whpg_query_history</structname> using SPI batch
   inserts of up to 256 rows per transaction.
  </para>

  <para>
   The table is created as a randomly distributed heap table during
   <command>initdb</command> (the <literal>DISTRIBUTED BY</literal> and
   append-optimized columnar storage options are not available in
   single-user initdb mode).  Operators can apply them post-initdb using
   <command>CREATE TABLE ... WITH (appendoptimized=true,
   orientation=column, compresstype=zstd) AS SELECT * FROM
   pg_catalog.whpg_query_history</command>.
  </para>

  <sect3 id="whpg-query-history-schema">
   <title>Schema</title>

   <programlisting>
CREATE TABLE pg_catalog.whpg_query_history (
    queryid                 int8        NOT NULL,
    session_id              int4        NOT NULL,
    command_count           int4        NOT NULL,
    backend_pid             int4        NOT NULL,
    dbid                    oid         NOT NULL,
    userid                  oid         NOT NULL,
    start_time              timestamptz NOT NULL,
    end_time                timestamptz NOT NULL,
    finish_status           text        NOT NULL,  -- 'ok', 'error'
    slice_id                int4        NOT NULL,
    segindex                int4        NOT NULL,  -- -1 = coordinator
    plan_node_id            int4        NOT NULL,
    parent_node_id          int4,                  -- NULL for root
    node_type               text        NOT NULL,
    actual_rows             int8,
    actual_ms               float8,
    execmem_bytes_peak      int8,
    workmem_bytes_peak      int8,
    spill_bytes             int8,
    bufusage_shared_hit     int8,
    bufusage_shared_read    int8,
    cpu_user_ms             float8,
    cpu_sys_ms              float8,
    trace_id                bytea
);
   </programlisting>
  </sect3>

  <sect3 id="whpg-query-history-summary">
   <title>Summary View</title>
   <para>
    <structname>pg_catalog.whpg_query_history_summary</structname>
    aggregates per-node rows to one row per query, providing
    <literal>duration_ms</literal>, <literal>total_rows</literal>,
    <literal>total_node_ms</literal>, and peak resource totals.
   </para>
  </sect3>

  <sect3 id="whpg-query-history-access">
   <title>Access Control</title>
   <para>
    <literal>REVOKE ALL ON pg_catalog.whpg_query_history FROM public</literal>
    is applied at <command>initdb</command> time.  Grant
    <literal>SELECT</literal> explicitly to monitoring roles.
   </para>
  </sect3>
 </sect2>

 <sect2 id="whpg-live-query-plan-gucs">
  <title>Configuration Parameters</title>

  <variablelist>
   <varlistentry id="guc-gp-enable-query-metrics">
    <term><varname>gp_enable_query_metrics</varname> (<type>boolean</type>)</term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Enables the shared-memory <structname>InstrumentationSlot</structname>
      ring that backs both the live view and the history table.
      Default: <literal>on</literal>.  Requires a server restart to take
      effect.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>

   <varlistentry id="guc-whpg-max-live-query-slots">
    <term><varname>whpg_max_live_query_slots</varname> (<type>integer</type>)</term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Number of plan-registry slots in shared memory.  Each slot stores
      the compact plan tree of one concurrently running query.
      <literal>0</literal> (default) uses <varname>max_connections</varname>.
      Requires a server restart to take effect.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>

   <varlistentry id="guc-whpg-avg-plan-bytes">
    <term><varname>whpg_avg_plan_bytes</varname> (<type>integer</type>)</term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Per-slot memory reserve in bytes for the plan registry arena.
      Default: <literal>131072</literal> (128 KiB).
      Requires a server restart to take effect.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>

   <varlistentry id="guc-whpg-query-history-enabled">
    <term><varname>whpg_query_history_enabled</varname> (<type>boolean</type>)</term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Master switch for end-of-query history persistence.
      Default: <literal>on</literal>.  Can be changed without a restart
      (<literal>PGC_SIGHUP</literal>).
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>

   <varlistentry id="guc-whpg-query-history-min-duration-ms">
    <term><varname>whpg_query_history_min_duration_ms</varname> (<type>integer</type>)</term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Only persist queries whose elapsed time exceeds this threshold
      (in milliseconds).  <literal>0</literal> (default) persists all
      queries.  Can be changed without a restart.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>

   <varlistentry id="guc-whpg-history-enqueue-timeout-ms">
    <term><varname>whpg_history_enqueue_timeout_ms</varname> (<type>integer</type>)</term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Milliseconds to wait for space in the history ring buffer before
      dropping rows.  Default: <literal>50</literal>.  Can be changed
      without a restart.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>
  </variablelist>
 </sect2>

 <sect2 id="whpg-live-query-plan-arch">
  <title>Architecture Notes</title>

  <para>
   The plan registry is a fixed-size shared-memory array of
   <structname>WhpgLiveQuerySlot</structname> entries, one per
   concurrently running query on the coordinator.  Each slot stores a
   compact serialization of up to <literal>WHPG_MAX_PLAN_NODES</literal>
   (1024) plan nodes.  Queries with larger plans are recorded with
   <literal>plan_truncated = true</literal> and a
   <literal>LOG</literal>-level message; they continue executing normally.
  </para>

  <para>
   The background worker (<literal>whpg history writer</literal>) connects
   to the database of the first queued entry and processes rows for that
   database.  In multi-database deployments, entries for other databases
   are logged and skipped; consider one coordinator per database for full
   history coverage.
  </para>
 </sect2>

</sect1>
